# Environments this repo creates: `.venv` is the documented CPU env (README), `.venv-rocm` is the
# separate AMD/ROCm env built by scripts/setup_rocm_windows.py (docs/gpu-reproduction.md).
.venv/
.venv-rocm/
# Guards for tool conventions this project does not use but a contributor might reach for
# (a different venv name, a setuptools build, coverage, tox/nox, mypy, a JS toolchain).
# None of these fire today; they are here so an accidental one is never committed.
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
.mypy_cache/
.cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
node_modules/

# `dist/` is not a wheel dir here: `git archive --format=zip -o dist/pop_repo.zip HEAD` builds the
# Colab payload there (docs/gpu-runbook.md). It is ~1.4 MB of the repo's own source, re-derivable
# from any commit, and must never be committed back into the repo it contains.
dist/

# mkdocs build output (`mkdocs build` -> ./site); regenerated from docs/ on demand.
site/

# caches / notebook checkpoints / stray logs
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.log

# Run artifacts. Every config writes its checkpoints under `outputs/<name>/` and the orchestrators
# (scripts/run_{training,rag,scaling}.py) write STATUS.md + per-step logs under `logs/`; on Colab
# both are symlinks into Google Drive. `wandb/` appears only when WANDB_API_KEY is set. All three
# are gigabytes of derived data whose committed summary is results/*.json.
outputs/
logs/
wandb/
# Local/ad-hoc runs. `pop smoke` and `pop execbench` default to `*_local*` names precisely so an
# ordinary run cannot overwrite a committed, published measurement -- write_results refuses to
# replace any *other* name. Their output is scratch, never a study result, so it is ignored.
# Keep this pattern in lockstep with `pop.eval.metrics.is_scratch_run_name`.
results/*_local*.json
# NOTE: results/scaling_data.csv and results/execbench_agreement.csv are the derived analysis CSVs.
# They are COMMITTED (not ignored): scripts/figures/make_all.py rebuilds them from the committed
# results/*.json before rendering, so the figures reproduce from a clean checkout without any
# fixture fallback.

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# model weights & archives - never belong in git (see docs/gpu-reproduction.md for where
# checkpoints live instead)
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.onnx
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
# ...but the vendored JUnit/Hamcrest jars are part of the execution harness and ARE tracked
!benchmarks/lib/*.jar

# secrets - real values stay local; .env.example is the committed template.
# Unlike the tooling guards above, this block is deliberately kept wide even where nothing
# matches today: a committed secret cannot be un-published, so the cost of a dead pattern
# here is a line of text and the cost of a missing one is a rotation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
.envrc
secrets.*
credentials.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
# SSH/GPG private keys carry no extension for `*.key` to catch.
id_rsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*.jks
*.keystore
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc

# local tool state - development-only, never part of the shipped project
.superpowers/
.autopilot/
.claude/
